{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#513","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#513","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#513\",\"parent_revision\":\"73161094c490fbfd9409f9a146c8446e881cf9a30336b22ce692ff7e14cb4dff\",\"root_revision\":\"73161094c490fbfd9409f9a146c8446e881cf9a30336b22ce692ff7e14cb4dff\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nIndividual backlog items are currently only accessible by calling backlog_view (a tool). MCP resources provide a read path that is separate from tools \u2014 clients can browse/read without consuming a tool call slot or triggering side effects.\\n\\nExpose each per-item file as a backlog://{slug} resource using @mcp.resource(\\\"backlog://{slug}\\\"). This gives clients (including Claude Code) direct access to item bodies without going through the tool layer.\\n\\nFiles affected: .claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py\\n\\nChanges required:\\n1. Add @mcp.resource(\\\"backlog://{slug}\\\") handler that reads the per-item file and returns its body as text\\n2. Add @mcp.resource(\\\"backlog://\\\") list handler returning all item slugs\\n\\nThis is additive \u2014 no existing tools change.\\n\\nSource: fastmcp v3 docs servers/resources.mdx \u2014 @mcp.resource for URI-addressed content\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 resource template pattern | AVAILABLE | Item description cites fastmcp v3 docs |\\n| 2 | Overlap with #466 (superset proposal) | AVAILABLE | Both propose backlog:// resources |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 but likely duplicate of #466. Resolve overlap before implementing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Trivial. Additive MCP surface. Potential duplicate of #466.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `@mcp.resource('backlog://{slug}')` handler reads the per-item file and returns its body as text\\n- `@mcp.resource('backlog://')` list handler returns all item slugs\\n- Resources are additive \u2014 no existing tools changed\\n- `uv run fastmcp list` shows both resource handlers\\n- Note: this item overlaps with #466 ('Expose backlog items and index as MCP resources in backlog_core') which proposes a superset. Recommend merging #513 into #466 or closing one as duplicate.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add @mcp.resource() handlers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 no change needed\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an MCP client, I need backlog items accessible via `backlog://{slug}` MCP resources so I can read item content without calling a tool and consuming a tool call slot.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **expose backlog items as mcp resources via backlog://{slug} uri scheme** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill analysis of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"92a91fc95ff191c8d3de586f8cc926338503272f1557a6b8a24ceee4c95a82dd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCucg\"}"}